This repository contains the core implementation of the methods presented in our
paper, "Topology-Preserving Scalar Field Optimization for Boundary-Conforming
Spiral Toolpaths on Multiply Connected Freeform Surfaces."

This project is developed by DexArcRobot (灵弧机器人), a research team at
Huazhong University of Science and Technology (HUST), led by Prof. Han Ding and
Prof. Xiaojian Zhang. Dr. Changqing Shen is responsible for algorithm
implementation and software development.

Our research focuses on robotic machining, geometric computing, and motion
planning. We apply geometric methods and optimization algorithms to improve the
efficiency and quality of machining complex surfaces.

By sharing our research code, we aim to support reproducible research, academic
exchange, and engineering applications. We welcome researchers and developers to
build upon, extend, and improve this work.

